        ]
      },
      "worked": "An integer divisible by both 8 and 20 is a multiple of their lowest common multiple. Let $N$ be the required number of positive integers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{lcm}(8,20)&=40\\\\N&=\\frac{1000}{40}\\\\N&=25\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are 25 positive integers satisfying both conditions.",
